%U A398465 119383666430739453576145920,5815284859101687785425920585728,617787469162744498307135910965497856,142171297682227522157040945186415192653824
%N A398465 Number of reducible flow graphs on n labeled nodes with entry node 1: digraphs in which every node is reachable from node 1 and every cycle has a unique entry node (Hecht-Ullman reducibility).
%C A398465 Reducible control-flow graphs on n labeled basic blocks, self-loops disallowed; multiply by 2^n to allow them (T1 ignores self-loops).
%C A398465 a(n) = 2^(n-1) times the global-source version (edges into the entry are always back edges, hence a free factor).
%C A398465 Computed by an exact recurrence system over the unique decomposition of a reducible flow graph into its strongly connected components: each SCC is a single-entry region (a strongly connected reducible flow graph), cross edges enter region headers only, and the region recursion counts single-source cores weighted by their sink SCCs.
%D A398465 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Flow graph reducibility, SIAM J. Comput. 1 (1972), 188-202.
%D A398465 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Characterizations of reducible flow graphs, J. ACM 21 (1974), 367-375.
%D A398465 R. W. Robinson, Counting digraphs with restrictions on the strong components, in T.-H. Ku (ed.), Combinatorics and Graph Theory '95, World Scientific, Singapore, 1995, pp. 343-354.
%D A398465 R. E. Tarjan, Testing flow graph reducibility, J. Comput. System Sci. 9 (1974), 355-365.
%H A398465 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A398465/a398465.py.txt">Python Program</a>, Jul 2026.
%F A398465 a(n) = Sum_{a=1..n} binomial(n-1,a-1) * W(a) * (reachable acyclic assemblies of reducible regions on the other n-a nodes), where W(m) is the strongly-connected rooted reducible count.
%F A398465 a(n) = 2^(n-1)*s(n), where s(n) counts the same reducible flow graphs with node 1 constrained to have indegree zero.
%o A398465 (Python) reducible_labeled_system(14)[0] # See link for program code.
%Y A398465 Cf. A396110 (all labeled entry-pointed digraphs), A351052 (all unlabeled entry-pointed digraphs).
%K A398465 nonn,new
%O A398465 1,2
%A A398465 _Gregory Morse_, Jul 30 2026
